    <li><strong>Prioritize Timing and Deadlines:</strong> Given the urgency level and potential financial hardships, adhere strictly to litigation timelines and court-imposed deadlines to avoid any adverse procedural impacts on the case.</li>
    <li><strong>Explore Settlement Options:</strong> Consider negotiating a settlement with the seller if substantial evidence suggests likelihood of success, thereby avoiding prolonged litigation. This strategy should be pursued if it aligns with the clients' financial and personal priorities.</li>
